course: dictionary
lesson: 7537
title: Precious words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Precious means very valuable, like «precious stones» such as diamonds and rubies. Gold and silver are precious metals because they are rare, so people pay a lot for them.
explain: Precious can also mean very important and loved. «Time is precious» means time is too valuable to waste. A precious toy is one you care about a great deal, even if it is not worth much money.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «A boy leaned on a glass case; it broke and a precious object was damaged.» A museum object that gets damaged is probably very valuable, so precious fits. Try the swap: "a valuable object was damaged" still makes sense.
explain: Be careful, because precious can be informal and mean too fussy or delicate. «Precious little» means very little. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning the author chose.
fact: Precious is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «precious stones».
fact: «Precious» means very valuable, worth a lot of money.
fact: «Precious» also means very important and loved, and not to be wasted or lost.
fact: «Precious little» is informal and means very little.
fact: Precious metals include gold, silver and platinum; they are rare and valuable.
exercise: «Gold and platinum are precious metals.» What does precious mean here? | Very wet | Very small | Very noisy | *Very valuable
exercise: «Time is precious, so do not waste it.» What does precious mean here? | Made of metal | Very loud | Very cheap | *Very important and not to be wasted
exercise: «Precious little» means what? | Very big | A lot of money | *Very little | Quite quick
test: «Her precious teddy bear went everywhere with her, because she loved it so much.» What does precious show? | The bear was very noisy | Her teddy bear was made of gold | *She cared about the bear very much | The bear was very cheap
test: «The Christians believe time can be a gift as precious as money.» What does precious mean? | Very old | Very wet | *Very valuable and important | Very small
exam: «The museum case broke, and a precious object was damaged.» Which word in the sentence tells you the object was very valuable? | *precious | case | museum | broke
